maintenance of rest. You can even take a

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:37.000
break for 15 seconds. We can all afford

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.160
to do that. The 2-minute reset between

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.880
tasks. So, this is slightly different

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.840
from a break. A break is you stepping

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.600
away, but a reset is simply you

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.840
transitioning to the next thing. So,

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.360
think about how you normally would go

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.720
through your day. You finish one task

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:50.640
and you immediately get into the next

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.720
thing, carrying the energy of the

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:54.600
previous task into the next one. For

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.120
example, if you feel frustrated from an

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.560
email, you bring that into your meeting

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.320
and then the stress from the meeting

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.040
follows you into your creative project.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.160
By the end of the day, you are just

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:05.400
carrying the residue of all that stress

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.120
from everything that you've done from

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.200
the day. So, try this out when you

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:11.400
finish one task. Before starting the

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.280
next one, just close your eyes and take

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.760
a few deep breaths. Place your hand on

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.200
your chest if it helps you stay more

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.880
present with your body and ask yourself,

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:20.480
"What do I actually need right now?"

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.760
Sometimes it may immediately come to you

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.120
and you think, "Oh, I need to go get a

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.680
glass of water. I need to stretch my

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.160
shoulders real quick. Oh, I need to let

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.840
go of that frustration from talking to

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:30.560
this person before I get on with the

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:32.440
rest of my day." Whatever it is, honor

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:34.520
that and think of it like clearing your

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:36.000
browser tabs. You wouldn't run 200

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.200
browser tabs and then wonder why your

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.560
laptop is being so slow, right? At the

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.400
end of the work day, if you're done with

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:43.200
everything, then you should get to close

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:45.200
your browser. It's the same thing that

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:48.040
we do with our own nervous system in our

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.839
bodies all day long. Plan your happy

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:52.839
moments. We plan so much of our lives,

00:10:50.839 --> 00:10:54.680
our goals, our projects, our work.

00:10:52.839 --> 00:10:57.000
Personally for me, because I'm low-key

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:59.320
insane, I plan my travel and my

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.160
vacations down to the hour sometimes

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.960
because I'm so passionate about it,

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.640
which is also why I'm such a great group

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.560
trip organizer. So, when was the last

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.839
time you actually sat down and planned

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.080
your joy? When was the last time you

00:11:08.839 --> 00:11:12.800
looked at your calendar and

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:15.120
intentionally scheduled a fun beach day

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:16.960
or hike or trip to the movie theater to

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:19.000
museum? If you've gone 7 days without a

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.280
single moment that gave you happiness

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.600
and joy, you're just existing and you're

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:24.960
not living your life fully. So, try this

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.760
once a week and this is something that I

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:28.960
actively have to do for myself, too.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:31.560
Plan something that's purely for your

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:33.160
own enjoyment, a nice dinner, a picnic,

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.040
plan your next vacation, something that

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:37.280
you get really excited about and gives

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:39.120
you a reason to look forward to instead

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:41.360
of just getting by and not knowing when

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:43.760
the next man-made horrors of living will

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:46.440
ever end. Joy doesn't just happen to

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.200
busy people. You have to schedule it in

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.120
and treat it like it matters as much as

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.760
your projects do because it does. It

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:54.040
might actually matter even more.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:56.360
Delegate what you can't do alone. I need

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.880
you to hear this from me. Delegation is

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:59.720
self-care and I know so many of you

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:01.600
pride yourselves on being the one who

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:03.200
can handle everything. I felt the same

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:05.480
way for the longest time. I think that I

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.120
can do anything and everything and I see

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:08.920
you and I love you. I know you can also

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:11.080
do anything, but we can't do everything,

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.600
right? So, think about one of the most

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.920
valuable things that people with a lot

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:17.600
of money buy. It's not material goods.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.480
The answer is actually more time. It's

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:21.640
buying time so that they can lower your

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:24.160
stress and relax and live your life and

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:25.920
be present with families and friends and

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.240
with themselves. Not everything needs to

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:30.240
be done by you. It can't be done by you

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.080
either, at least not without a cost. For

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.920
example, even though I love planning

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:35.640
group trips, my group trips take a huge

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.600
amount of coordination and they're a lot

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:39.440
of work. I don't have decades of travel

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:40.920
agency experience behind me and all I

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.480
have is I know I'm an amazing trip

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.920
planner. So, I have planned many trips

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.680
for myself, my friends, and my family

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:47.480
before. I know I'm really good at it. My

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.760
last trip to Crete went really well and

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:50.360
now we're about to go island hopping

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:52.320
again in the Greek Islands. So, I

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:54.200
realized after a while that even though

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:56.280
I love it so much, it definitely does

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:58.880
take time away from me. It also adds to

00:12:56.280 --> 00:13:01.080
my stress and I can't do this alone. I

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:03.120
should be able to just show up and be

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.280
the host of my trip instead of being the

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:07.200
organizer and the host and the

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:09.360
coordinator and the customer service

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:12.200
representative. I need to understand my

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:14.440
role better and fully be the host and

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:16.320
give everyone a great time. The most

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:18.920
successful and powerful women that I

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:21.839
know all have one thing in common. They

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:24.520
learn how to receive. Accepting help is

00:13:21.839 --> 00:13:26.400
not weakness, but it is wisdom. If you

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:28.720
can afford to outsource something or

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.720
delegate something that drains you, do

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.240
that. You can ask someone for help with

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:34.360
something that you know that they're

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.800
better than you at. You can admit that

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:37.160
to yourself and then you can ask them

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.760
for help. More than likely they will be

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.560
willing to help you. For example, that's

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:43.280
what I do between me and my robot vacuum

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:45.600
and I ask it for help and it helps me

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:46.960
clean my house every day. So, identify

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.800
one thing this week that you've been

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:50.640
white knuckling all on your own and let

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.840
someone else hold your hand with you.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.960
Maybe have them do it because they're

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:55.520
better at it than you are. Just try one

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:57.320
thing out and notice how you feel when

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:59.280
you can release that grip of controlling

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:01.600
everything in your life. Curate your

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:03.120
media consumption. Your nervous system

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.120
does not know the difference between

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:07.200
your real life and the content that

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:09.480
you're consuming. So, your body

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.400
processes a scary movie the same way

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:13.240
that it processes a real threat because

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:15.080
your brain doesn't add a little note

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.680
that says, "Oh, this is fictional, so

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.080
don't worry so much about it." Your

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:19.840
heart rate still increases, you feel

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:21.560
nervous, your muscles tense up while

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:23.640
you're watching a scary movie, and you

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.920
feel more stressed. I used to love

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:26.440
watching thrillers and I thought they

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.400
were so fun and entertaining, but then I

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:30.520
started to pay attention to how I

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.680
actually felt after watching them and I

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:35.400
noticed after watching a thriller or

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:38.360
horror movie, my sleep becomes worse, my

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:40.080
anxiety is higher, and I'm just on edge

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:42.880
and in fight or flight mode all day

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:44.800
long. Basically, chronic low-grade

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:47.800
stress mode all the time and I was

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:50.120
choosing to do this voluntarily for fun.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:52.040
Same thing with video games. I used to

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:53.960
play a lot of video games. I noticed

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:56.160
that it was keeping me in the same fight

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:58.240
or flight mode, just being stressed out

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.880
and I wasn't able to sleep at night.

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:02.200
After a while, I realized it actually

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:04.760
really did add to my anxiety, so I made

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:06.960
the change to stop consuming content

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:08.360
that put my body in a stress response.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:10.880
The difference actually is very

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:13.520
noticeable. I feel like my whole life is

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:15.400
more calmer and more peaceful. I sleep

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:17.680
better now. I'm not creating fake danger

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.440
in my body all the time. So, audit what

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:21.160
you're consuming. What are you watching?

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:23.160
What are you listening to and scrolling

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:25.240
through? And ask yourself, does this

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:27.240
nourish me or deplete me? You don't have

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.800
to cut everything out. I watch plenty of

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:30.680
things like funny cat video

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:33.160
compilations. I have my own comfort

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:35.400
YouTubers I love watching as well, but

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:37.320
swap one chaotic input for one that

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:39.120
actually supports your growth and gives

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:40.880
you more peace and makes you happier and

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.880
healthier. Maybe it's to unfollow

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:44.680
certain accounts that spread unnecessary

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:46.400
fear and add more stress to your life

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:47.960
because if you're protecting your energy

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:50.240
and what you're doing with your time,

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:52.200
let's also protect what you're consuming

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:55.320
as well. Meditation and nervous system

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:56.960
regulation. I saved the best for last on

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:58.920
purpose because I think that a lot of

00:15:56.960 --> 00:16:01.040
people do this wrong or they think that

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:02.120
it doesn't matter enough. Meditation is

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.400
not about clearing your head of

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:04.640
thoughts. You know, a lot of people

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.840
think they fail at it because their

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:07.040
brain wouldn't shut up and you get

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.880
intrusive thoughts and all of that.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:10.600
Meditation's actually about building a

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:13.000
personal relationship with your nervous

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:15.560
system and noticing when you're shut

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:17.720
down and when you are actually regulated

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:20.160
and you're present and you feel good.

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:22.760
Over time, you will learn how to more

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:24.839
consciously choose what state you get to

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:26.560
be in instead of losing control and

00:16:24.839 --> 00:16:28.040
being at the mercy of whatever happens

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:29.839
to you, which is why I'm building my

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:32.400
Stoic Angels membership platform. It's

00:16:29.839 --> 00:16:34.360
own stand-alone 2.0 platform. Eventually

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:36.080
will be an app because I realized that

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.880
most people have never been taught how

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:40.280
to regulate the nervous system and this

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:41.720
takes practice. You have to do it and

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:43.720
not just think a thought and then

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:46.040
something magically happens. It takes

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:48.400
actual somatic body-based practices to

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:50.040
help you shift from being neurotic, aka

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:52.120
being all up in your head and over

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:54.320
thinking, and channel it out through

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:56.880
your body so that we get to live in our

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:59.160
bodies. That is how we get to think more

00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:01.400
clearly and respond better instead of

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:03.200
reacting and stressing ourselves out for

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.360
no reason. Inside my new membership

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.480
platform, I'm going to guide you through

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:09.000
nervous system regulation practices,

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:10.240
meditations, deep inner work that makes

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.839
all of these other macro habits

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:14.360
sustainable for you because they have

00:17:11.839 --> 00:17:16.400
been for me for years and they've really

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:18.040
been a safety net for me. You can do all

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:20.240
of these nine points correctly, but if

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:21.920
your nervous system is still stuck in

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:24.120
chronic stress mode, you won't be

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:25.720
getting the full benefits as you should.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.760
The inner work is actually what makes

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:28.960
that outer work stick. So, if this

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:30.640
resonates with you, you can join the

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:32.360
waitlist the link in my description and

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:34.280
sign up for my newsletter so that you

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:36.600
can be the first to hear about it.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:38.600
Angels, I have to remind you self-care

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:40.800
is not a luxury or something that you

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:42.600
have to earn. It's not selfish. It's not

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:44.640
frivolous. It is essential and the

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.240
foundation of everything else and I wish

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.360
they taught us this in school because

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:50.400
they don't. All of these things will sit

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:52.280
on other things like how well you take

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:54.480
care of yourself, your body, your mind,

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:56.680
and your spirit. It doesn't have to be

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:58.920
hard either. You already do a lot of

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:01.160
these things day-to-day on autopilot and

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:03.560
all we have to do are these minor little

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:05.040
tweaks here and there, beneficial

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:07.320
add-ons that create something even

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:09.720
better for you in the long run. You also

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:11.360
do not have to try everything at once.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:13.400
You start with a couple and then you try

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:15.040
another, try the ones that you like, the

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.720
ones that you think you need, and get

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:18.560
rid of the ones that you don't like. So,

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:21.440
if you're still here, comment with me

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:23.360
and affirm, I am in my self-care era. I

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:25.760
read all your comments and I'm affirming

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:28.120
this alongside you. I love you, angel. I

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:30.920
believe in you and I will see you in the

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.920
next video.

